      <h3 id="stig-profiles_compliance-operator-supported-profiles" class="group scroll-mt-20 small">STIG compliance profiles<a href="#stig-profiles_compliance-operator-supported-profiles" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
      <Alert variant="info" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Important</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>Applying automatic remediations to any profile, such as <code>rhcos4-stig</code>, that uses the <code>service-sshd-disabled</code> rule, automatically disables the <code>sshd</code> service. This situation blocks SSH access to control plane nodes and compute nodes. To keep the SSH access enabled, create a <code>TailoredProfile</code> object and set the <code>rhcos4-service-sshd-disabled</code> rule value for the <code>disableRules</code> parameter.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
